<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "Lincoln worked on the speech in the weeks before November 19, 1863; a Library of Congress copy begins in ink on Executive Mansion stationery written in Washington, and the drafts are in steady handwriting unlike a moving train's." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "Lincoln dashed off the Gettysburg Address on the back of an envelope on the train to Gettysburg." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "The envelope story turns a carefully revised speech into a lucky improvisation and hides how deliberately Lincoln shaped his public words." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did Lincoln win the presidency in 1860 with less than 40 percent of the popular vote?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Four major candidates split the vote; Lincoln carried every free state, which gave him 180 of 303 electoral votes, a clear Electoral College majority, even though he was not on the ballot in much of the South." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the actions of enslaved people shape Lincoln's emancipation policy, according to historians such as Ira Berlin?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "By fleeing to Union lines and offering labor and military service, enslaved people forced Union officers, Congress and the president to decide their status; Lincoln, who had first favored gradual, compensated emancipation and colonization, moved toward the Emancipation Proclamation as that pressure grew." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why do historians debate Lincoln's title of \"Great Emancipator\"?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Some see his leadership as the decisive force that ended slavery, while others argue he was a reluctant emancipator and that enslaved people were the prime movers; the debate is about how to weigh presidential leadership against the agency of the enslaved." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/abraham-lincoln> .
