<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/jim-crow-laws> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The state and local laws, backed by custom and violence, that enforced racial segregation and stripped Black Americans of voting rights, mainly in the South and border states, from the end of Reconstruction until federal laws and court rulings dismantled them in the 1950s and 1960s." .
