<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/voting-rights-act-of-1965> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The federal statute, signed by President Lyndon B. Johnson on August 6, 1965, that enforced the Fifteenth Amendment by banning racial discrimination in voting nationwide, outlawing literacy tests, and placing jurisdictions with a record of disenfranchisement under federal registration and \"preclearance\" oversight." .
